    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Commissioning of a 500-kV substation at Dasht-e-Alwan 
Indicator: Transmission flow capacity between north and south Afghanistan increased from 300 MW in 2012 to 1,300 MW completed 
Progress/Status: The 500/220kV Dasht-e-Alwan (Pul-e-Khumri) substation contract was awarded to KEC International on 13 January 2016. The overall progress is 100%. The project civil works, electrical and erection/installation work has been completed.  The project closing date was 7 January 2019. DABS has issued the Project Completion Certificate dated 4 January 2019 against contractor&amp;apos;s commitment letter. The hot commissioning will be done once the 500kV TL from Turkmenistan is connected with the substation. 
Data Source: Afghanistan CSO publications

DABS annual report

Publication by International development partners

AEIC online reports 
