   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Outcome</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable power supply in northern, eastern and southern Afghanistan</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">NEPS capable to supply 150 MW in 2009 to 1,450 MW of connected load by 2020 
Progress/Status: The project added transmission line capacity up to 300 MW. Various donors along with ADB are implementing respective programs to extend NEPS&amp;apos; capacity and strengthen institutional arrangements for Operations and Management (O&amp;M) of power infrastructure in Afghanistan. The physical work of 600 km of 500kV power transmission line connecting the TKM to AFG grid is under construction starting from TKM border till Kabul with expected completion by 2021. When completed the power transmission capacity will increase to 1,300MW. The 500kV substation will be further upgraded to expand its capacity under North-South Additional Financing. The 500kV power transmission line connecting the UZB to AFG contract will be awarded by Q4, 2020. By completion of this line, the power transmission capacity will be further increased to 2,300 MW. 
Data Source: Afghanistan CSO publications

Publications by international development partners

DABS annual report

AEIC online reports 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
